This was caused by the exact same WSL IPv6 routing issue as before, but this time it was happening at the Root Server level!

If you remember, earlier I added the 13 IPv6 Root Servers to the root_servers.c list, bringing the total to 26 root servers (13 IPv4 and 13 IPv6).

When you typed your dig commands, the daemon randomly selected one of those 26 servers to start its search:

When you queried neverssl.com AAAA, it randomly picked an IPv4 root server, successfully contacted it, and did the full recursive loop in 126msec.
When you queried neverssl.com A, it randomly picked an IPv6 root server. Because your WSL network can't reach IPv6 addresses, it immediately crashed with Network is unreachable and returned NXDOMAIN in 0msec.
It was essentially a 50/50 Russian Roulette whether a query would fail instantly or succeed!

The Fix
I just reverted src/root_servers.c to only contain the original 13 IPv4 Root Servers.

I have compiled the fix for you, so if you restart your daemon again (wsl ./dns_resolver), you will find that neverssl.com A works perfectly every single time!